# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/out/
*.local.json

# Reviewer / agent scratch directories. These hold throwaway CLI fixtures
# (IR JSON, generated VSDX, exported models) produced while verifying behaviour.
# They must never be committed: `git add -A` will otherwise sweep them in.
# Reviewer scratch dirs, one per review round. Use a pattern rather than listing
# each round: forgetting to add r5 is exactly how 297 files got committed once.
# Every reviewer scratch directory, not just the one name that was current when this rule was
# written. `.review-rv` and `.review-final` were both committed — 1265 files, 5.7 MB — because the
# rule listed `.review-scratch*/` and the directories were named something else.
.review*/
.review-scratch*/
/.sm/
/.rv*/
/.[a-z][0-9]*/
.p9/
.lab/
.scratch/
*.review.json

# Single-letter dot directories. Verification steps create short-lived fixtures in these
# (`mkdir -p .d`, `.v`, `.q` …) and `git add -A` swept 13 of them into history once already.
# A pattern beats a list: the previous round-by-round enumeration missed r5 and let 297 files in.
/.[a-z]/
